{"prototypeToken":{"displayName":20,"displayBars":20,"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"height":1,"width":1,"name":"Contortion Crown","actorLink":false,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/tokens/contortion-crown.webp","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"tint":"#ffffff","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"fit":"contain","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1},"negative":false,"priority":0},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":{},"randomImg":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/subjects/contortion-crown.webp"}},"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null,"depth":1},"name":"Contortion Crown","type":"npc","effects":[],"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":265,"temp":0,"max":265,"details":""},"ac":{"value":32,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":25,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"weaknesses":[]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["aklo","common","sakvroth"],"details":""},"level":{"value":12},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>A contortion creeper grows slowly as it ages and amasses a collection of pilfered items within its extradimensional space. Magical items within the collection accelerate the process as their power permeates into the creature's body. The rare few that accumulate such a hoard become a massive and dangerous creature that can rapidly conquer a village or small town. Once a creeper becomes large enough to inhabit a small building, insatiable greed drives it to seize any and all objects within its ever-growing reach. Wagons, livestock, monuments, marketplaces, and even small ships become new additions to its hoard. Such a powerful creeper transitions from dwelling to dwelling, driving out inhabitants powerless to stop it. Folk unable to combat the monstrosity must evacuate their homes and eventually abandon their village, which the creeper claims as its dominion. Such tragedies earn this type of creeper the title contortion crown.</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Contortions are a family of aberrations that share a distinctive behavior: like hermit crabs, they find and inhabit discarded objects, which they use as dwellings to protect their vulnerable bodies from harm. However, unlike hermit crabs, contortions tend to inhabit junk found in humanoid settlements rather than shells on the beach. Like hermit crabs, contortions continue to grow and trade up to larger and larger dwellings. While the smallest might live in a shoe, the largest are big enough to inhabit small buildings.</p>\n<h2>Contortion Colonies</h2>\n<p>When a mature contortion creeper or contortion crown comes across a large enough quantity of junk, the glee from this new treasure trove causes polyps to swell up around the base of their arms. Eventually, these polyps explode, releasing a small colony of infant contortions. The members of the colony inhabit the smaller pieces of junk until they grow enough to form a contortion swarm.</p>\n<h2>Crown Collaborations</h2>\n<p>Up to three contortion crowns can collectively dominate an abandoned village or small town, which becomes overrun with their spawn, consisting of contortion swarms and smaller creepers. Each new contortion creeper is born inside an object belonging to its parents' collection. The greed of a contortion crown eventually drives its young out of the home to seek treasures elsewhere. Towns inhabited by multiple contortion crowns often devolve into political battlegrounds between the enormous tyrants.</p>\n<h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2>\n<p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 250/560/1,030 gp</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Athletics, Society, Stealth, Thievery)</p>\n<p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> bane, constitution, elongating, energy resistant (positive), intelligence, strength, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Strange and Unusual","authors":"Garrick J. Williams","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"creatureType":""},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":7},"dex":{"mod":4},"con":{"mod":7},"int":{"mod":5},"wis":{"mod":2},"cha":{"mod":4}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":20,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":19,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":25},"stealth":{"base":22},"thievery":{"base":25},"society":{"base":20}},"traits":{"value":["aberration"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"grg"}}},"img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-su-pf2e/art/Portraits/contortion-crown.webp","items":[{"type":"action","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","name":"Improvised Block","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The contortion crown would take damage while Inhabiting an object</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The crown wards off the blow with its improvised carapace. The object's Hardness prevents up to 15 damage. The crown and the object both take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the object and expelling the crown. The object has 60 Hit Points and a Break Threshold of 30.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"","_migration":{"version":0.932,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.853,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"category":"defensive","actions":{"value":""},"deathNote":false,"requirements":{"value":""},"trigger":{"value":""}},"effects":[],"_id":"iWd58yTQGZqddOY2","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.0.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1687303827233,"modifiedTime":1687304534495,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","name":"Junk Carapace","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"gdgVt6BtUnm4mvK4":{"damage":"3d10+13","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":26},"attackEffects":{"value":["improved-push"]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"_migration":{"version":0.932,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"12.328","system":"6.1.0"}}},"effects":[],"_id":"WnhE88fzFxTy8AVe","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"5.0.1","coreVersion":"14.360","createdTime":1687303954800,"modifiedTime":1687304961511,"lastModifiedBy":"W75cDAmGcgt3X6Rq","compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null}},{"type":"melee","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/melee.svg","name":"Limb","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"value":["reach-20","sweep"],"otherTags":[]},"damageRolls":{"c3whACi9tywx1mM6":{"damage":"3d10+13","damageType":"bludgeoning","category":null}},"bonus":{"value":26},"attackEffects":{"value":[]},"publicat